(General-purpose M6 ngc= procedure -- the safe default for any machine)
(without a real automatic turret or carousel -- most probe_basic lathe)
(users, doing a manual tool change. Calling M6 again from inside the)
(M6 remap's own ngc= procedure is LinuxCNC's documented mechanism for)
(use-the-builtin-behavior -- see LinuxCNC's own gmoccapy reference)
(config, configs/sim/gmoccapy/macros/change.ngc: manual tool change)
(prompts the operator and waits exactly as it always did with no remap)
(at all -- a random-toolchanger setup gets its own stock handling too.)
(change_prolog and change_epilog in stdglue.py still run around this)
(call -- that is what publishes #<_current_tool_*> after every tool)
(change, regardless of tool-change hardware.)

(Machines with a REAL automatic tool changer should point)
([RS274NGC] REMAP=M6 ... ngc= at toolchange instead of)
(toolchange_manual -- that file implements actual carousel or turret)
(indexing, rotate, clamp, unclamp, position-sensor checks, and is NOT)
(a safe default for a manual machine.)

o<toolchange_manual> sub

o100 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    (PRINT, o<toolchange_manual>: task is null)
    o<toolchange_manual> return [999]
o100 endif

M6

o<toolchange_manual> endsub [1]

M2
